# Plan (opus, strong)

## Goal

In the deck editor, each deck-list tile for a card that the validator's verdict names (L3, L5, L6, L7) gets three things:
- a `data-issue="<rule>"` attribute;
- the validator's translated sentence in its `title` and `aria-label`;
- the existing `db-tile-flag` mark, in the verdict's amber.

A card that also clashes with a compared deck gives both reasons. Errors with no `cardId` (L2) stay only in the verdict box. With no collection, `deckVerdict` already treats every card as owned (`ownershipUnknown`, `apps/web/src/game/deckbuilder/workshop.ts:87-105`), so no L5 mark can appear. Every new string gets a `zh-CN.json` entry. The client only shows what the validator decided (CLAUDE.md rule 7).

## Files to touch

| Path | Kind | What changes |
|---|---|---|
| `apps/web/src/game/deckbuilder/DeckEditor.tsx` | change | Import type `LoadoutError`. New memo `cardIssues` (card id → first error naming it). Pass `issues={cardIssues}` to `DeckSidebar`. |
| `apps/web/src/game/deckbuilder/DeckSidebar.tsx` | change | `DeckSidebarProps.issues`, `DeckTileProps.issue`. `DeckTile` gets `data-issue`, a combined `aria-label` and `title`, and the flag when there is a conflict or an issue. Header comment line. |
| `apps/web/src/game/deckbuilder/deckbuilder.css` | change | Two rules: `.db-tile[data-issue]` edge and `.db-tile[data-issue] .db-tile-flag` tone. |
| `apps/web/src/i18n/zh-CN.json` | change | Three new entries after `"Also in {deck}"` (line 194). |
| `apps/web/src/game/deckbuilder/DeckWorkshop.test.tsx` | change | New `describe` block with four tests. |

Do not touch:
- `crates/` (the validator is read only);
- `spec/`, which needs no ruling: §9.4's L1–L7 and R253 govern this, read only;
- `crates/cards/patches/`, which needs no fragment because no card plays differently;
- `testids.ts`, because test ids stay;
- `TrioEditor.tsx`, `workshop.ts`, `docs/`, `e2e/`;
- `.github/`, `.harness/`, `.squishy/`, `bot/`.

## Steps

1. **`DeckEditor.tsx`, imports (line 15).** Change it to `import type { CatalogSnapshot, Collection, LoadoutError } from "@jackioh/validator";`.

2. **`DeckEditor.tsx`, new memo.** Put it right after the `verdict` `useMemo` (it ends at line 187), before `const code = …`:
   ```ts
   // The verdict's first error naming each card, for that card's tile; one naming no card (L2) stays in
   // the verdict box only. The tile shows the validator's words and checks nothing (CLAUDE.md rule 7).
   const cardIssues = useMemo(() => {
     const named = new Map<string, LoadoutError>();
     if (verdict.ok) return named;
     for (const issue of verdict.errors) {
       if (issue.cardId !== undefined && !named.has(issue.cardId)) named.set(issue.cardId, issue);
     }
     return named;
   }, [verdict]);
   ```

3. **`DeckEditor.tsx`, the `<DeckSidebar` element (line 377).** Add the prop `issues={cardIssues}` on the line after `conflicts={conflicts}`.

4. **`DeckSidebar.tsx`, imports and props.**
   - Line 15 becomes `import type { CatalogSnapshot, LoadoutError } from "@jackioh/validator";`.
   - In `DeckSidebarProps`, after `conflicts`, add:
     ```ts
     /** The verdict's first error naming each card (DeckEditor's `cardIssues`), shown on its tile. */
     issues: ReadonlyMap<string, LoadoutError>;
     ```
   - In `DeckTileProps`, after `conflict`, add `issue: LoadoutError | undefined;`.

